WEBVTT
 
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.250
Dominoes Quick Starter. The Skateboarder by Christine Lindop.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:26.574
Chapter 1. No skateboard

00:00:26.635 --> 00:00:33.470
Near Hannah's house, there's a new skatepark.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:41.818
A lot of young people in the town go there after school with their skateboards.

00:00:41.878 --> 00:00:48.964
These days Hannah often goes there with her cousin, Justin.

00:00:49.024 --> 00:00:53.029
Justin goes to school with her.

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:59.832
Hannah doesn't like school very much, or getting up early.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:07.434
She's always late, and she doesn't have many friends.

00:01:07.494 --> 00:01:16.156
But with the new skatepark, she's suddenly very interested in skateboarding.

00:01:16.216 --> 00:01:27.666
The only thing is – Hannah has no skateboard! Sometimes Justin asks Hannah,

00:01:27.726 --> 00:01:32.428
Hey, do you want to get on my skateboard?

00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:35.150
So she does.

00:01:35.209 --> 00:01:38.952
But not for long.

00:01:39.012 --> 00:01:45.304
She doesn't want to fall off in front of everybody.

00:01:45.364 --> 00:01:50.974
So usually she watches the skateboarders.

00:01:51.034 --> 00:01:54.473
Owen is 15.

00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:57.464
He's a good skateboarder.

00:01:57.524 --> 00:02:02.526
He can do a lot of tricks.

00:02:02.586 --> 00:02:09.648
I love Owen's skateboarding. Hannah thinks.
 
00:02:09.708 --> 00:02:14.720
I want to jump and do tricks too.

00:02:14.779 --> 00:02:19.111
Why don't you have a skateboard, Hannah?

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:21.218
Justin asks her.

00:02:21.278 --> 00:02:27.700
It's a new thing for me. Skateboarding. Hannah answers.
  
00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.992
Then she thinks.

00:02:30.052 --> 00:02:32.485
My birthday's coming.

00:02:32.545 --> 00:02:48.450
Maybe I can talk to Mom and Dad.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:03:09.900
Chapter 2. Good grades, better presents. 

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:17.471
On Hannah's birthday morning, she opens her presents.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:22.916
There's a big present from her mother and father.

00:03:22.975 --> 00:03:28.630
Hannah opens it first, excitedly.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:36.085
Wow! She cries. A skateboard! Thanks.
 
00:03:36.145 --> 00:03:41.669
Well, your school grades are good, Hannah.

00:03:41.729 --> 00:03:43.760
Her mother says.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.037
And it is your birthday.

00:03:47.097 --> 00:03:51.233
Now open that present,

00:03:51.293 --> 00:03:54.854
Now, open that present.

00:03:54.914 --> 00:03:59.224
Her father says, it's from Evan.

00:03:59.284 --> 00:04:02.085
Hannah opens it.

00:04:02.145 --> 00:04:04.846
It's a helmet.

00:04:04.906 --> 00:04:06.776
Awesome!

00:04:06.836 --> 00:04:13.494
Hannah cries, but her older brother, Evan, laughs.

00:04:13.554 --> 00:04:18.842
You like watching skateboarding videos, I know.

00:04:18.902 --> 00:04:24.863
He says, but do you, uh, skateboard?

00:04:24.923 --> 00:04:29.694
Yes, I do. Hannah says hotly.
 
00:04:29.754 --> 00:04:41.914
Sometimes – on Justin’s skateboard! And I have my skateboard now, so I can do more.

00:04:41.974 --> 00:04:47.264
Can you jump or do tricks? Evan asks.
 
00:04:47.324 --> 00:04:51.238
Can you go fast and stay on?

00:04:51.298 --> 00:04:52.709
Duh!

00:04:52.769 --> 00:04:56.252
Hannah answers her brother angrily.

00:04:56.312 --> 00:04:59.424
What dumb questions!

00:04:59.484 --> 00:05:03.828
Evan, honey, please.

00:05:03.888 --> 00:05:09.291
Their mother says, it's Hannah's birthday.

00:05:09.351 --> 00:05:14.102
Okay, Evan says.

00:05:14.162 --> 00:05:22.934
That weekend, Hannah takes her new skateboard to the skatepark with Justin.

00:05:22.994 --> 00:05:26.186
There aren't many people there.

00:05:26.246 --> 00:05:29.648
Hannah is excited.

00:05:29.708 --> 00:05:32.958
Okay, let's go.

00:05:33.018 --> 00:05:39.334
Justin says, The two cousins begin skateboarding.

00:05:39.393 --> 00:05:42.756
Justin does a trick.

00:05:42.816 --> 00:05:47.390
Hannah skateboards up and down.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:51.103
Maybe I can jump now.

00:05:51.163 --> 00:05:53.074
She thinks.

00:05:53.134 --> 00:05:55.706
She goes faster.

00:05:55.766 --> 00:05:59.279
Then she jumps.

00:05:59.339 --> 00:06:04.667
But she falls off her skateboard.

00:06:04.727 --> 00:06:10.752
When Hannah is on the ground, somebody laughs.

00:06:10.812 --> 00:06:15.100
Oh no, they're laughing at me.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.246
This is awful. She thinks.
 
00:06:19.306 --> 00:06:22.637
She gets up quickly.

00:06:22.697 --> 00:06:24.708
I'm going.

00:06:24.768 --> 00:06:29.410
She tells Justin, and she leaves.
 
00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:35.027
Just then, Owen arrives with his friends.

00:06:35.087 --> 00:06:41.306
They're laughing at a picture of Owen on his phone.

00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:45.388
But Hannah's far away now.

00:06:45.448 --> 00:06:48.960
No more skateboarding for me.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:07:02.000
She thinks.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:22.600
Chapter 3. First steps. 

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:28.414
The next day, Justin stays at home with his family.

00:07:28.474 --> 00:07:32.752
But Hannah walks past the skatepark.

00:07:32.811 --> 00:07:37.238
A lot of people are doing tricks.

00:07:37.298 --> 00:07:43.330
I can't skateboard there now.Hannah thinks.
 
00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:47.572
She watches Owen on his skateboard.

00:07:47.632 --> 00:07:52.803
He goes up in the air and comes down again.

00:07:52.863 --> 00:07:56.964
He's awesome. Hannah thinks.
 
00:07:57.024 --> 00:07:59.782
And I'm awful.

00:07:59.842 --> 00:08:07.023
She leaves the skatepark and begins to walk home through the park.

00:08:07.082 --> 00:08:10.084
The sun is hot.

00:08:10.143 --> 00:08:14.815
Hannah sits down on one of the park benches.

00:08:14.875 --> 00:08:21.348
The sun is in her eyes, so she closes them.

00:08:21.407 --> 00:08:28.709
When she opens her eyes again, she sees a young woman near her.

00:08:28.769 --> 00:08:33.781
She is sitting on the grass with her baby boy.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:39.263
The little boy is trying to stand.

00:08:39.323 --> 00:08:43.226
Good boy, Michael.

00:08:43.286 --> 00:08:51.870
His mother says, stand up now. Yes, that's right.
 
00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:55.938
Michael stands up slowly.

00:08:55.998 --> 00:09:00.587
He takes one little step and falls down.

00:09:00.607 --> 00:09:05.840
Oh, come on now, Michael.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.952
His mother says, don't cry.

00:09:10.012 --> 00:09:12.694
Try again.

00:09:12.754 --> 00:09:17.416
Michael stops crying and laughs.

00:09:17.476 --> 00:09:22.680
He takes his mother's hand and stands up again.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:28.504
Good boy, Michael. His mother says.
 
00:09:28.564 --> 00:09:32.194
Michael sits down suddenly.

00:09:32.254 --> 00:09:37.925
He laughs and claps his hands happily.

00:09:37.985 --> 00:09:43.406
Hannah watches them for five minutes.

00:09:43.466 --> 00:09:50.300
Michael stands up and falls down again and again.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:57.554
Try again, Michael. His mother says.
 
00:09:57.614 --> 00:10:00.916
He doesn't stop falling.

00:10:00.976 --> 00:10:06.009
But it doesn't matter. Hannah thinks.
 
00:10:06.069 --> 00:10:12.634
He gets up and tries again. Time after time.
 
00:10:12.694 --> 00:10:16.416
And he's no more than a baby.

00:10:16.436 --> 00:10:21.690
Hannah leaves the park and walks home.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:25.505
She thinks about baby Michael.

00:10:25.565 --> 00:10:32.650
OK, she says. I need some more skateboard practice. 

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:48.600
But where can I go for that?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:11:10.900
Chapter 4. Practice, practice, practice. 

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:19.603
Hmm. Let's see. The skatepark’s no good, Hannah thinks.
  
00:11:19.662 --> 00:11:23.704
I want to do my practice alone.

00:11:23.764 --> 00:11:28.494
That evening, she goes for a walk.

00:11:28.554 --> 00:11:33.966
Two blocks from her house, there's an office building.

00:11:34.026 --> 00:11:39.890
At half past five, everybody in it goes home.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:46.834
They drive all their cars out of the parking lot.

00:11:46.894 --> 00:11:54.938
Hey, I can skateboard here. Hannah thinks.
 
00:11:54.998 --> 00:12:02.330
The next evening, she takes her skateboard and helmet with her.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:06.492
I'm going out for some skateboard practice.

00:12:06.552 --> 00:12:08.600
she tells her mother. 

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:13.522
She skateboards to the parking lot.

00:12:13.582 --> 00:12:16.884
There are no cars there.

00:12:16.944 --> 00:12:21.356
First, she skateboards slowly.

00:12:21.416 --> 00:12:26.738
She is alone and nobody is watching.

00:12:26.798 --> 00:12:31.981
This is awesome. She thinks.
 
00:12:32.041 --> 00:12:37.220
After an hour, she goes home.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:41.580
She skateboards most evenings.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:45.914
Soon she can go fast.

00:12:45.974 --> 00:12:50.828
One evening she tries jumping.

00:12:50.888 --> 00:12:58.165
She skateboards across the parking lot and jumps.

00:12:58.225 --> 00:13:05.069
Suddenly she is on the ground.

00:13:05.129 --> 00:13:10.710
A woman is going past on a bicycle.

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:16.643
She sees Hannah on the ground and smiles at her.

00:13:16.703 --> 00:13:18.644
Bad luck!

00:13:18.704 --> 00:13:22.695
She calls, try again!

00:13:22.755 --> 00:13:32.008
So Hannah tries once more and falls off her skateboard again.

00:13:32.068 --> 00:13:39.038
She laughs, gets up and goes home.

00:13:39.098 --> 00:13:45.531
Two days later, Hannah is back in the parking lot.

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:50.593
She jumps again.

00:13:50.653 --> 00:13:58.156
This time, she doesn't fall off.

00:13:58.216 --> 00:14:03.400
At home that evening, her mother says, 

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:07.462
You're happy about something, honey?

00:14:07.522 --> 00:14:08.952
Tell me.

00:14:09.012 --> 00:14:10.983
What is it?

00:14:11.043 --> 00:14:14.514
Well... Hannah begins.
 
00:14:14.574 --> 00:14:17.096
Don't laugh, okay?

00:14:17.156 --> 00:14:18.706
Okay.

00:14:18.766 --> 00:14:21.998
The practice is helping.

00:14:22.058 --> 00:14:28.400
I can do good skateboard jumps now. Usually.
 
00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:32.405
That's wonderful, honey.

00:14:32.465 --> 00:14:36.779
Just then, Evan comes in.

00:14:36.839 --> 00:14:40.170
Oh no. Hannah thinks.
 
00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:55.000
What does he want?

00:14:55.100 --> 00:15:14.800
Chapter 5. Up early. 

00:14:14.900 --> 00:15:19.206
Hey, how’s your new skateboard?

00:15:19.266 --> 00:15:22.718
Evan asks Hannah nicely.

00:15:22.778 --> 00:15:26.291
Their mother smiles at this.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:30.343
Then she quickly leaves the room.

00:15:30.403 --> 00:15:35.826
Oh, it's not bad. Hannah answers.
 
00:15:35.887 --> 00:15:38.909
And the helmet's awesome too.

00:15:38.969 --> 00:15:42.202
But I have a lot of bruises now.

00:15:42.262 --> 00:15:43.652
Look.

00:15:43.712 --> 00:15:49.424
Evan looks at the bruises all over her arms and legs.

00:15:49.484 --> 00:15:52.185
Ouch! He says.
 
00:15:52.245 --> 00:15:56.697
So, do you skateboard at the skatepark now?

00:15:56.757 --> 00:15:59.848
No. Hannah answers.
 
00:15:59.908 --> 00:16:03.880
There are always a lot of people there.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:07.422
But I want to go up the walls.

00:16:07.482 --> 00:16:11.199
I want to turn in the air too.

00:16:11.259 --> 00:16:17.710
Well, I go past the skatepark every day when I go to work.

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:21.112
There's nobody there in the early morning.

00:16:21.172 --> 00:16:27.086
Evan says, Evan, that's an awesome idea.

00:16:27.146 --> 00:16:28.998
Hannah cries.

00:16:29.058 --> 00:16:32.380
I can go there before school.

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:34.442
Thanks.

00:16:34.502 --> 00:16:40.062
Next day, Hannah gets up at six o'clock.

00:16:40.123 --> 00:16:45.114
She skateboards for an hour before school.

00:16:45.174 --> 00:16:48.106
This is wonderful.

00:16:48.166 --> 00:16:51.358
Her mother says a week later.

00:16:51.418 --> 00:16:56.122
Hannah's up early every morning these days.

00:16:56.182 --> 00:17:00.366
She's never late for school now.

00:17:00.426 --> 00:17:05.129
Sometimes Hannah is tired in the morning.

00:17:05.189 --> 00:17:09.592
But then she remembers baby Michael.

00:17:09.652 --> 00:17:14.024
Babies get up early. She thinks.
 
00:17:14.084 --> 00:17:18.956
So I can get up early, too.

00:17:19.016 --> 00:17:26.930
One Saturday afternoon, her cousin Justin calls her on the phone.

00:17:26.991 --> 00:17:28.731
Hey, Hannah.

00:17:28.792 --> 00:17:30.902
Are you coming tomorrow?

00:17:30.962 --> 00:17:34.654
Coming where? What's tomorrow?
 
00:17:34.714 --> 00:17:37.196
It's June 21st.

00:17:37.256 --> 00:17:39.910
Go Skateboarding Day.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:45.317
People all around the world are skateboarding.

00:17:45.377 --> 00:17:49.960
I'm going to the skatepark with all my friends.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.782
Come with us.

00:17:51.842 -->  00:17:54.875
Okay. Hannah says.
 
00:17:54.934 --> 00:17:56.405
See you there.

00:17:56.466 --> 00:17:59.398
Don't forget your skateboard.

00:17:59.458 --> 00:18:00.850
Justin says.

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:18.800
Justin, don't be dumb. Hannah answers.
 
00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:40.050
Chapter 6. A real skateboarder
 
00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:43.616
It's June 21st.

00:18:43.676 --> 00:18:47.874
Hannah finds her skateboard and helmet.

00:18:47.934 --> 00:18:51.492
Then, she goes to the skatepark.

00:18:51.552 --> 00:18:54.084
She's excited.

00:18:54.144 --> 00:18:56.544
Can I do this?

00:18:56.604 --> 00:18:58.726
She thinks.

00:18:58.786 --> 00:19:03.200
I don't know, but I can try.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:09.750
At the skatepark, Hannah sees Justin with some friends.

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:12.670
She goes over to them.

00:19:12.731 --> 00:19:18.114
Hey, Hannah! Justin says, Watch this.
 
00:19:18.174 --> 00:19:22.348
Owen's doing a very tough trick.

00:19:22.408 --> 00:19:26.702
Owen goes up the wall and turns.

00:19:26.762 --> 00:19:29.704
He goes very high.

00:19:29.764 --> 00:19:33.498
Everybody stops and watches.

00:19:33.558 --> 00:19:35.329
Wow!

00:19:35.389 --> 00:19:39.703
Hannah says, he's awesome.

00:19:39.763 --> 00:19:43.896
Owen does a different trick now.

00:19:43.956 --> 00:19:52.578
It's an easy trick, but this time he falls off his skateboard.

00:19:52.638 --> 00:19:58.031
He walks past Hannah and smiles at her.

00:19:58.091 --> 00:20:01.002
Everybody falls off sometimes.

00:20:01.062 --> 00:20:02.673
Owen says.

00:20:02.733 --> 00:20:06.206
Sure. Hannah answers.
 
00:20:06.266 --> 00:20:09.120
How do you do that trick?

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:11.202
I want to learn it.

00:20:11.262 --> 00:20:13.694
Put your right foot here.

00:20:13.754 --> 00:20:15.335
Owen tells her.

00:20:15.395 --> 00:20:18.548
Then push with your left foot.

00:20:18.608 --> 00:20:22.200
Owen helps Hannah with the trick.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:25.584
Okay. Hannah says.
 
00:20:25.644 --> 00:20:30.228
I need some more practice with that, but thanks.

00:20:30.288 --> 00:20:34.259
You're a real skateboarder now, Hannah.

00:20:34.319 --> 00:20:39.179
Justin tells her quietly after that.

00:20:39.239 --> 00:20:46.372
Later, Hannah and Justin walk home through the park.

00:20:46.433 --> 00:20:50.604
Hannah sees baby Michael again.

00:20:50.664 --> 00:20:56.036
He is walking across the grass to his mother.

00:20:56.096 --> 00:21:04.519
This time, he doesn't take her hand, and he doesn't fall down.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:08.230
Hello. Says Hannah.
 
00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.880
She smiles at him.

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:13.931
Can you do it again?

00:21:13.991 --> 00:21:16.382
Says Michael's mother.

00:21:16.442 --> 00:21:25.364
The baby laughs and claps his hands. And again.
 
00:21:25.424 --> 00:21:30.305
he says, and he stands up.

00:21:30.365 --> 00:21:35.014
Justin and Hannah walk away.

00:21:35.074 --> 00:21:39.364
Who's that? Justin asks.
 
00:21:39.424 --> 00:21:45.862
Now? Oh, a little baby. Hannah answers.
  
00:21:45.922 --> 00:22:09.000
But maybe one day, a really good skateboarder!
